Job Description

At GroundIQ, we are transforming how engineers understand the subsurface. By combining advanced ground imaging with geotechnical data, we help engineers make faster, smarter decisions about what lies beneath. As part of Fugro, we combine the reliability and expertise of a global leader with the innovation and agility of a forward-thinking technology team.

We are looking for a Scientific Product Engineer who can bridge the gap between science and product development. In this role, you will take cutting-edge scientific research, algorithms, and models and turn them into reliable software solutions that engineers use on real-world infrastructure projects.

Your role

You translate scientific research, algorithms, and prototypes into reliable product features that deliver value to engineers;
You own features end-to-end, from defining problems and validating solutions to measuring real-world impact;
You collaborate with users and stakeholders to understand needs, prioritise development, and ensure scientific rigor where it matters most;
You work across the technology stack, from frontend and backend development to cloud infrastructure, scientific computing, and machine learning;
You optimise and scale solutions, including performance-critical components where required;
You leverage AI-powered tools to enhance development speed, quality, and productivity;
You balance scientific excellence with product delivery, while actively sharing knowledge and supporting team growth. 


Your track record

You have a strong academic background in Physics, Applied Mathematics, Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, typically at MSc or PhD level;
You have 4+ years of experience building and delivering software products with end-to-end ownership;
You have successfully transformed scientific research, algorithms, or prototypes into production-ready solutions;
You are experienced across the technology stack, with strong expertise in Python and scientific computing;
You have excellent analytical and problem-solving skills and thrive in ambiguous, research-driven environments;
You leverage AI tools to improve productivity and quality, while bringing a pragmatic, collaborative, and user-focused mindset. 


What Fugro Offers

A diverse and inclusive working environment;
A competitive salary;
29 holidays per year based on a fulltime employment (of which 4 are appointed by Fugro management) and the possibility to purchase 12 additional days; 
Extensive career & training opportunities both nationally and internationally;
Flexible working hours and the ability to work from home in accordance with your manager and corporate policies; 
Commuting allowance;
Modern pension scheme;
Collective health insurance;
Possibility to register with our corporate fitness plan;
Coaching options through our EAP (Employee Assistance Program). 


Are you interested?

Please visit our Company Page to find out more about what it is like to work at Fugro.

For further information, please contact Stefanie Baldassarri-Steenhauer, Senior Talent Acquisition Partner, tel. +31 (0)6-114 55954.

After you have applied

You will receive an automated confirmation-email of the receipt of your application. 
When we see a match, we will invite you for the first interview within a couple of days. Of course, you will also receive a message if we will not invite you; 
After a successful first round, you will be invited for the second round. 
If we are both still positive after the second interview, we will make you an offer, and with that we hope to welcome you to Fugro! 


Disclaimer For Recruitment Agencies

Fugro does not accept any unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies. Acquisition to Fugro Recruitment or any Fugro employee is not appreciated.

